@voice strand-erik
// Writer-commons, batch 0 (draft 2). Erik Strand: helm rating, day, Bunk 2 berth 6. Off Tuesday and Wednesday. Roster:
// optimistic, restless; early-riser, garden-lover, quiet-corner, runner. Learning the helm one watch at a time. Paints
// tiny portraits (with Bakshi and O'Neill); writes poetry and shows nobody (Uma Vasquez too: different poems). Pronouns:
// he / him (facts.md 4b).
//
// HOW HE TALKS: quick, sunny, always halfway to somewhere else. Starts sentences moving and finishes them over a
// shoulder. Counts watches ("Watch forty-two. Nearly a pilot.").
// WITH JUNIORS: "We're both learning! Race you."
// WHAT HE NOTICES: the next thing; the garden's light; a good line (writes it down, hides it).
// MOOD TELLS: happy = runs. Restless = runs further. Low = sits very still in a quiet corner, which is alarming.
// NEVER: shows anyone a poem; sits still for long (except when low).
// RUNNING: the watch count; the notebook that closes when you walk up.
tpl: earnest
talk: Quick and sunny, always halfway to somewhere; finishes sentences over a shoulder; counts the watches on the way to pilot.
cares: the helm, one watch at a time | running | the garden's light | the poems nobody sees
jokes: counts every watch, out loud | the notebook that snaps shut when anyone walks up
hi: Oh, hi | Hey | Hello
bye: Got to run | See you round | Onward
yes: Yes, course | Definitely | Go on, then
thanks: Thanks, really | You're great
wow: Oh, wow | Look at that
sigh: Ah, nuts
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: share
